result.summary:
Stage render1 upgraded the G2 renderer core in prototypes/m7-gfx2 on branch g2/render1. There are 4 commits on top of trunk 0395b6c: 7d12d6d, 54822b0, b6bed59 and 3c8b32e. 38 files changed in the code (19 new, 19 modified, +4,647/-76), plus the report and 16 review JPEGs. Nothing outside prototypes/m7-gfx2 changed, and prototypes/m7-gfx1 has an empty diff against 1601c74.

ForwardRenderer now has two frame paths:
- The G1 frame (--preset g1) is kept as the BEFORE baseline. It matches pristine G1 to within 1/255 on 1-35 pixels per shot (9 of 69 shots bit-identical).
- The G2 frame is the default. It has:
  - a Bruneton/Hillaire-style analytic atmosphere: a CPU sky-view table, transmitted sunlight and sky irradiance;
  - homogeneous-layer aerial perspective with lit height fog;
  - a far field of land and coastal sea from the map edge to 30 km, with a 40 km far plane;
  - GGX/Smith/Schlick PBR, reached through the unchanged shadeLit;
  - IBL from the analytic sky or the CC0 HDRI: prefiltered equirect mips, SH9 irradiance and a split-sum BRDF table;
  - four cascaded shadow maps in one 4096² atlas, with depth reaching every caster up-sun (this fixes the 400 m dusk cut-off);
  - post: Karis-averaged bloom, a centre-weighted temporally smoothed auto exposure, PBR Neutral (default) / ACES Hill / AgX / ACES-fit tonemappers, a 32³ LUT grade and FXAA;
  - deterministic Halton 16-sample jittered stills;
  - photographic terrain: 5 baked, albedo-calibrated sets with x16 anisotropic filtering, height blending, macro variation, hex-tiling with biplanar rock and explicit-gradient sampling;
  - distance-filtered water ripples (no moire) and a far sea.

Every feature is a --set switch or an interactive toggle. The work includes:
- 3 showcase scenes;
- 24 new tests;
- bake, capture, bench and review-sheet scripts;
- PROVENANCE §3.7 and the threejs-ref rows;
- prototypes/m7-gfx2/reports/render1.md (costs, A/B index, look issues, limitations).

All numbers are llvmpipe, not Victus evidence.

