KitTests cover:
- socket placement (hip on the pelvis, near the hip joint and away from the hand; forearm, back and head) over all 10 identities;
- strap fit (fist within 30 mm of the hand grip for the aspis, and for the kite with a 28 mm stand-off);
- finger wrap (no joint inside the shaft, error under 15 mm, curl shrinks with grip thickness);
- central-grip spin;
- generator determinism and seed variation;
- well-formed meshes and maps for every kind;
- normal-map convention and height-to-normal sign;
- PNG round trip;
- hero glTF byte-identical and round-tripping;
- authored clips reaching their hand targets (2 cm, 5°), deterministic, deaths lying flat and surrender kneeling;
- helmets hiding hair but not the face;
- carried scabbard hanging from hip_l;
- bow string length kept while the limbs bend;
- DR42: no reference to a Sim.* or Proto* assembly;
- a device still rendering the bronze aspis.

During the run the tests caught three defects, all fixed: a zero normal in the great helm, a forward death propped up by a hand pushed into the ground, and the scene test asserting a draw count it never started counting.

